    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1059">

                <pb facs="1092" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6311/251</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-18T21:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 18, 1916, 9 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 19, 9.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1749. My 1744, December 14, 3 p. m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1059-f1"/> Have just
                    learned at Foreign Office that the French Government will accord safe-conduct
                    for Count Tarnowski and suite.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
